          "revision": "sha256:6f8a19b4b97612857818d6782d60f23e3519b6b9d55e4981e34c48843fba21fa"
        }
      ],
      "purpose": "Check the limit of the first result.",
      "explanation": "At Δ=1, E=2, ε=1/4 and δ=3/4, the exposition gives v3 ≤ 5/32 < 4/25 < v2 and V₂(3,S) < V₂(2,S) for 0≤S≤9/400. Thus the adjacent smaller batch can win at positive calibrated noise. The transcript brackets and inclusive energy range have the supplied formal bindings. The average-only reversal is a separate conventional extension. The lower comparator is the squared Gaussian base standard deviation, identified with full batch through the fullbatch target.",
